-- ============================================================
-- ASSIGNMENTS (active and returned)
-- Note: Karen Brown (emp-11, inactive) and Leo Nguyen (emp-12, inactive)
-- each have active assignments to trigger offboarding alerts.
-- Partial unique index allows only one active assignment per asset for
-- non-license assets, but license assets can have many (seat-based).
-- ============================================================

-- Drop and recreate partial unique index to allow license multi-assignment during seed
-- The partial unique index on assignments (asset_id) WHERE returned_at IS NULL 
-- only allows one active row per asset_id — this works for single-assignment assets.
-- For license assets, we need multiple active assignments. We'll handle this by
-- removing the unique index and relying on app logic, OR we accept that the unique
-- index means we can only seed one active assignment per license asset.
-- Design says partial unique enforces FR-2 (single active per non-license).
-- Since we can't conditionally exclude license assets from a partial index easily,
-- let's seed one active assignment per physical asset and multiple returned ones.

